{"id": "EUVD-2026-103623", "enisaUuid": "3b484e27-bf79-330a-bc80-ea548c0f0dd4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: st21nfca: validate ISO15693 inventory length\n\nThe ISO15693 inventory helper removes a two-byte prefix without checking\nthat it exists, then accepts a one-byte remainder before reading data[1] as\nthe DSFID.\n\nRequire the prefix and at least two remaining bytes before copying the UID\ndata and reading the DSFID.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e47b2a350bb0ff123434ec5484c6dc3333b0727c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/57d183764f3002f9625ee4deeeb20716c519534e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3af2ea4035581a1607d9830779c187a0c7e225aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fa21b0f78adb514e3bd96a505ddb752e9727ff3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6353dae51bc9b3cad13c9d890b53311a46c96b4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdd95e819d828c975aaeb258a3fed5dd7fd136d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a86987d03a4d39acdbe4533d83db4d656ea36c59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f2ea5ed588c03d481f0301e6c3d4240132383fb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mm2q-hf2x-48gq", "CVE-2026-98578"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0936599e-02eb-3f2d-b76d-9626f825c970", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "17a416d1-1cc6-35b4-b346-ccd8a1305556", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "1c2d9640-248b-3cff-8cf9-feceb1b1fc46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7974728094d35f38775417a26d8f30ea3602496a <57d183764f3002f9625ee4deeeb20716c519534e"}, {"id": "29556ad9-a820-3601-b6df-4d71b182e434", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7974728094d35f38775417a26d8f30ea3602496a <a86987d03a4d39